      "writtenOn": "2025-03-14T15:45:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be better to switch this from SerialQueue to some kind ordered map. If you have say 3 deallocations for the serial 2 then SerialQueue will hold `{2, {1000, 200, 600}` That requires a vector to store the individual sizes when you just need the sum. You can sum up all of the deallocations and store `{2, 1800}` in a map. Pushing deallocations into the map is is just `mDeallocatedHeapAllocations[serial] +\u003d size` and with an order map you can iterate up a serial.\n\nThere is a SerialMap but it holds `std::map\u003cSerial, std::vector\u003cValue\u003e\u003e`. It would be easy enough to implement a SerialStorage specializaton where `Storage` is defined as `std::map\u003cSerial, Value\u003e` and `Enque()` adds to the value if you felt like it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 324,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 324,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "a696d5029be6cbe350dd45d17faa865a455c54b1",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
